{"text": "LISA HERBOLD\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nJanuary 2016\nCurrent\n\nJanuary 1998 ~\nDecember 2015\n\nMay 1997 ~\nNovember 1997\n\nSpring 1993 ~ May\n1997\n\n\u2018Summer 1992~\nSpring 1993\n\nFall 1989 \u2014\n\u2018Summer 1992\n\n\u2018Spring 1989 Fall\n1989\n\nVOLUNTEER\n\nBoard of\n\ntors\n\nEDUCATION\n\n1984-1989\n\nCity Councilmember, District 1, West Seattle and South Park, City of Seattle\n\n+ Helped craft and pass public policy that includes Paid Sick Leave for the 190,000 Seattle\n\u2018workers who didn\u2019t have it, 2 Rental Housing Inspection Program for 250,000 renter\nhouseholds, andthe pilot project for LEAD, an acclaimed criminal justice diversion program.\n\nLegislative Aide, The Office Of Councilmember Nick Licato, City Counel, ity of Seattle\n+ Policy analysis, development, and implementation, project management, constituent\nand press relations, annual newsletter editor, and scheduling\nCampaign Coordinator, People for Nick Licata\n\nResponsible for coordination of all aspects of campaign, from volunteer recruitment and\nsupervision, event planning, press relations, strategy and tactics, and materials\ndevelopment.\n\n\u2018Tenant Organizer, Seattle Tenants! Union\n\n+ Stafed a statewide tenants\u2019 rights hotline, conducted trainings for advocacy organizations\n\u2018on tenants rights, bringing groups of tenants together in their buildings towards collective\naction on issues of common concern whether focused upon changes to their individual\ntenancy or towards larger policy changes.\n\nLead Organizer, Association for Community Organization for Reform Now (ACORN)\n\n\u201c Managed, with the Head Organizer, al aspects of launching a new Seattle office and from\nthe ground up, building a staff, organizational infrastructure, and a membership base where\nthere had been none.\n\nSouthside Organizer, Syracuse United Neighbors (SUN)\n\n- Responsible for managing membership group of 400 individuals, monthly and bi-monthly\n\u2018meetings, as well a neighborhood issue-based campaigns, including press relations and\nleadership development\n\nCanvass Director, Syracuse New York Public Interest Research Group (NYPIRG)\n\nHired, trained, and supervised canvassing staff of ~ 20 as well as managing all aspects ofthe\nsummer canvass, from maintaining financial records, on-going reporting to State\nheadquarters, to managing the day-to-day operations of a busy office\n\nHomestead Community Land Trust (1997 - 1999), Young Adult Independent Living\nProgram (1998 ~ 2000), Neighborhood House 2004-2006, The Tenants Union 2006 -\n2010\n\nSyracuse University, Political Science/Journalism",
